    "description": "## Ask\n\nAfter BUILD-272 deploys, fill missing field values on existing Deals and regenerate their Names and External Deal IDs so every record matches the current derivation. 26 of 28 Deals have a blank Source and ids with no source suffix, so almost every deal would be rejected by the CMS as a makeup mismatch. Requested by Emily (Slack, 2026-09-08).\n\n## Target\n\n1. **Fill the gaps first** — `Source__c` on every non-test Deal, plus any blank `Market_Country__c` / `Market_State__c` / `Partner__c`. Values from WagerTech, not inference (one Deal is currently named `-PULSZ-CTM-CASINO-TEST`, a blank-market record).\n2. **Names regenerate themselves** — the Deal Name flow fires on create and update with no entry filter, so a touch-save is enough.\n3. **External Deal IDs need an explicit clear** — null the field on the affected non-test Deals and save; BUILD-272's Decision restamps from the current makeup.\n4. **Exclude** `Test_Deal__c` **= true from the CMS sync** — the `TEST-` prefix can never match the CMS derivation. Write that exclusion into the sync ticket's acceptance criteria.\n\n> This window closes at first sync. Once a deal has synced, its identity is locked and the only correction path is Retire & Replace, which costs a record and its history.\n\n## Done when\n\n* `Makeup_Drift__c` is FALSE on every non-test Deal, with one hand-check per region/vertical/source combination in use against the CMS webhook guide section 2 derivation.\n* No Deal Name has a leading hyphen or an empty segment.\n* Test Deals are excluded from the sync scope, recorded on the sync ticket.\n* No Deal has synced before this pass completes.\n\n",
